ForeRSI is a recursive self-improvement (RSI) framework built on agent teams that explore approaches in parallel, execute plans, and use feedback from verification to guide the next iteration.

- The Coordinator shares the agreed task and any changes with the team.
- Explorers send proposals to Checkers for review. Workers implement approved proposals and hand the implementation back to Explorers to check against the proposal.
- Verifiers evaluate candidates against the task’s criteria and record results to guide the next round of exploration.
- The Watchdog flags stalls, repeated work, and handoff problems to the teammates who can address them.

Read “The improvement loop” in ForeRSI’s `README.md` to see how the team turns verification results into the next round of work and how the Watchdog helps improve the workflow.
